  "description": "The proposal is for replacement of steel-framed, single-glazed Crittal windows and patio doors of an existing flat with white uPVC double-glazed windows to kitchen, bathroom, bedroom, and windows and patio doors to reception room. The proposed replacement windows and doors will be in designed to match the profile and design of the majority of existing units within the building. Planning permission has been granted for similar replacements in other flats in the block (including applications 2023/2261, 2023/1917, 2022/1451 and 2018/1737) and the proposal will maintain a consistent and uniform appearance across the building. \n\nThe replacement door and windows would broadly match the profile and design of the existing windows/doors of the property. The proposal would also utilise the existing window openings to maintain the existing fenestration arrangement (except for the insertion of a small top-hung casement window within the bathroom window arrangement to improve ventilation and to match neighbouring properties in the block) and as such there would be no significant change in appearance to the host building. The change to uPVC materials would not harm the visual amenity of the building which is not listed or within a conservation area. The proposed openings would be no larger than existing and no extensions are proposed; there would be no loss of light, outlook or privacy to adjoining properties.\n\nPlease see attached documents.",
